/a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say get it now. Even if you just get to read the intro fiction, it's awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you've convinced me.<br /> <br /> By the way, does anyone know which artist did the picture that comes right after the opening fiction? I really like the work they've done for Chronicles of Darkness books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T12:47:12-08:00","id":1265357,"title":"","content":"Been so waiting for this. I hope you all enjoy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Rick A. Carroll - Onyx Path Freelancer</b><br /> <b>Worked On</b>: Night Horrors: Enemy Action, Night Horrors: The Tormented<br /> <b>Working On: </b>Nada at the moment. Hire me!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2737-thrazghul","name":"Thrazghul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T13:21:41-08:00","id":1265367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1265275-night-horrors-the-tormented-on-dtrpg?p=1265287#post1265287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hollow got updated Bestowments for 2e!</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's a new Zeka Bestowment... given to one of the last Zeky who'd want it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T14:36:32-08:00","id":1265385,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that the Zeka are <i>hilariously </i>powerful, especially while in Torment (they get a boost nearly equivalent with Going Loud, which is scary), but the drawback is that they need radiation, and lots of it, to recharge where a more standard Promethean can do so simply. Fortunately, their Disquiet causes radiation. Getting attacked while using Transhuman Potential causes radiation. Basically, the Zeka are incentivized to poison people with radiation and hang around them to watch the fallout to heal and recharge.<br /> <br /> Oh, they can also cause severe Disquiet without a Wasteland, and their Disquiet adds the distinctly disturbing option of escalating violence in increasingly drastic manners to &quot;burn it off&quot;. Oh, did I mention that their Disquiet can be passed by <i>touch</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-07T15:10:06-08:00","id":1265390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1265275-night-horrors-the-tormented-on-dtrpg?p=1265385#post1265385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be noted that the Zeka are <i>hilariously </i>powerful, especially while in Torment (they get a boost nearly equivalent with Going Loud, which is scary), but the drawback is that they need radiation, and lots of it, to recharge where a more standard Promethean can do so simply. Fortunately, their Disquiet causes radiation. Getting attacked while using Transhuman Potential causes radiation. Basically, the Zeka are incentivized to poison people with radiation and hang around them to watch the fallout to heal and recharge.<br /> <br /> Oh, they can also cause severe Disquiet without a Wasteland, and their Disquiet adds the distinctly disturbing option of escalating violence in increasingly drastic manners to &quot;burn it off&quot;. Oh, did I mention that their Disquiet can be passed by <i>touch</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>So what you're saying is...<br /> <br /> Mission accomplished on making the mere presence of a Zeka ridiculously dangerous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh